# Design-system quality bar and gates

A new or modified design-system package is complete only when **all** of the following are
true:

- Typed props with explicit variant unions (no free-form `string` variants).
- Token-driven colors and spacing — zero hard-coded values.
- Accessibility-first defaults (`development/05-accessibility.mdc`).
- Storybook covers every variant and state listed in
  `design-system/02-package-conventions.mdc`.
- A doc page exists under `docs/design-system/components/` and is linked from the
  design-system index.
- Colocated Jest tests exist for every extractable piece of pure logic.

## Pure logic inside design-system packages

Behavior expressible without React — layout math, token resolution, a11y string
composition, badge scaling — lives in a colocated `*.ts` + `*.test.ts` pair.

- **Storybook does not replace Jest** for these rules.
- Presentational-only components may omit component-level Jest when Storybook covers the
  surface; smoke tests are welcome but optional.
- A `styled.ts` containing only static declarations needs no standalone test — until logic
  is added to it.
- Inside a package: **relative imports** between siblings — never the package's own alias
  barrel (circular-dependency risk).

## Required validation (before merge)

Run the scoped gate whenever design-system packages or theme tokens change:

```bash
npx eslint "src/components/**/*.{ts,tsx}" "src/theme/**/*.{ts,tsx}"
npx tsc --noEmit --pretty false
```

Both must be clean, fixed in the same work cycle. CI is a backstop, not the gate.

## Color governance

Use the existing palette first. New tokens only when the current set cannot model the use
case, added with a clear semantic name (role-based, not appearance-based: `inkPrimary`,
not `darkGray`).

## In-app component lab (recommended)

Keep a `__DEV__`-only test screen that exercises global overlays (toasts, modals, icon
fonts) inside the real app shell on all platforms. Extend it whenever a new global overlay
primitive or modal variant is added — Storybook cannot validate provider wiring.
